# Optional. Overrides the values in src/lib/supabase-config.js without
# editing that file - e.g. to point a local checkout at a different Supabase
# project. Copy this file to .env and fill in your own project's values
# (Supabase dashboard -> Project Settings -> API). Neither value is secret.
#
# IMPORTANT: use the "anon" / "public" key here - never the "service_role"
# key. service_role bypasses every Row Level Security policy in
# supabase/schema.sql; putting it in a VITE_ variable ships it to every
# visitor's browser, in plain sight, as full read/write access to the whole
# database. If it ever ends up in a file like this one, rotate it
# immediately (Supabase dashboard -> Project Settings -> API -> "Reset
# service_role secret") - a key that has already touched disk or been shared
# should be treated as burned, not just replaced going forward.
#
# If you'd rather not use an env file at all, just fill in PROJECT_URL /
# ANON_KEY directly in src/lib/supabase-config.js instead - see that file.

VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
